--
std::bind (libstdc++ _Bind / _Bind_helper machinery): free function with
bound arguments, free function with a placeholder, and a member function
pointer with an object pointer and a placeholder.  Exercises the
function-type pack-expansion pattern of _Bind_helper, the base-specifier
pack expansion of result_of<F(A...)>, the empty-pack-then-defaulted
_Result parameter of _Bind::operator(), the zipped type/index pack
expansion of _Bind::__call, pointer-to-member deduction through
__result_of_memfun<_Res _Class::*, ...> and (*p).*pmf on a reference
result.  Conversion of a _Bind to std::function is a separate, still open
layer (the goto-symex shadow_memoryt dog-food carrier).
